## 8. Why L1 gives enormous NPG

L1 compresses an astronomical number of microscopic degrees of freedom into a few macroscopic variables.

For \(N \sim 10^{23}\) particles:

\[
K(\text{microstate}) \gg K(T, P, V, S)
\]

Yet these macroscopic variables predict behavior extremely well.

Thus:

\[
\mathrm{NPG}_{L1}
=
\frac{L(\text{micro-baseline}) - L(\text{thermo-model})}
{L(\text{micro-baseline})}
\gg 0
\]

This makes thermodynamics one of the highest-gain levels in the UAF hierarchy.

